he may have landed the  park six weeks went by which caused  holland to lose hope but sure enough he  was flown back out to atlanta to do a  screen test with evans after weeks of  not hearing back he assumed that he lost  the part until one fateful day when he  saw an instagram post from marvel i type  in marvel  i've still got the article saved on my  computer i did it and it says we would  like to introduce our new spider-man tom  holland i ran downstairs i was telling  my i got it i got it i got the park got  the park  zendaya initially didn't know she was  auditioning for a brand new spider-man  pick with the casting call vaguely  calling for a girl in movie i didn't  even know what kind of character i was  going to play till like i got there and  got to sign this non-disclosure her  auditions went flawlessly holland  recalled that the producers knew right  away that they found their mj she came  in and they cast her before she even  left the room  upon dropping out of college in hawaii  batalon found himself a talent agent who  advised him to join the new year  conservatory for dramatic arts he  initially didn't even have much of an  interest in acting i want to be a  musician at first i when i was going to  college on hawaii i was studying music  theory but then i dropped out and then  acting just kind of happened for me film  school made me really maybe really  appreciate filmmaking during his final  year he did his very first audition  sending in a self-taped submission for a  supporting role in a marvel movie never  thinking it'd go anywhere as faye would  tell batolon received a callback and was  flown out to burbank to perform a screen  test with tom holland batalon described  the audition as nerve-wracking stating  that tom had a really good time but i  was shaking in my shoes but it was  really fun  gyllenhaal has gone on record to say  that it's the character driven films  like donnie darko and nightcrawler that  have attracted him the most when  gyllenhaal received a call from far from  home director john watts about  potentially playing the role of mysterio  he stated that he had to do his research  first to see if it'd be the kind of role  that he's keen on playing that has  always been my desire to find something  in that space that seems to match my  skill and also what i love and my own  honesty and it just so happened that it  does with that part revelry initially  auditioned to play the web head himself  since the casting call was open to any  ethnicity he claimed that while it was  fun he felt like he botched his audition  he would later return to audition for  the role of ned getting called back  multiple times before the producers  realized they had another role in mind  for him flash thompson revolori wasn't  told the name of the character and was  told to recite the lines of biff tannin  from back to the future as a comic book  fan he ultimately put two and two  together and realized that he was  actually auditioning for flash  tomei initially wasn't aware of the  ant-may character in the comics and went  through the entire negotiation talks not  knowing her character was traditionally  depicted as a senior citizen tomei  claims she was horrified upon learning  more about the character she and the  producers initially considered giving  her character her traditional silver  locks before ultimately going a  completely new route with the character  that tomei would be more comfortable  playing  from the time the creative team behind  homecoming decided that vulture would be  the villain they knew right away which  actor they wanted to portray the classic  spider-man foe michael keaton  surprisingly kitten almost wasn't cast  in the role as talks initially fell  through due to scheduling conflicts in  the end keaton did land the part and now  it's hard to picture anybody else in the  role of the winged villain  his audition process didn't last nearly  as long as some of his other co-stars  when it came 